            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Erwin Chemerinsky (Petitioner), the injunction at issue is alleged to violate the First Amendment because it is a prior restraint and a content\u2011based restriction on speech."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Erwin Chemerinsky (Petitioner)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13a32e8e68ccccbb35b57c0dfbbfbd31b1625a257effdab4aaf267306aa623c0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13a32e8e68cc-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "13a32e8e68ccccbb35b57c0dfbbfbd31b1625a257effdab4aaf267306aa623c0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13a32e8e68cc-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Erwin Chemerinsky (Petitioner), the petitioner argues the injunction is overbroad, restricting speech of non\u2011parties."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Cole",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13a32e8e68ccccbb35b57c0dfbbfbd31b1625a257effdab4aaf267306aa623c0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13a32e8e68cc-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Cole, the respondent contends that the conduct of attempting to extort money is not protected speech."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Cole",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13a32e8e68ccccbb35b57c0dfbbfbd31b1625a257effdab4aaf267306aa623c0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13a32e8e68cc-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Cole, the respondent argues California does not adopt the collateral bar rule; People v. Gonzales supports this position."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Cole",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13a32e8e68ccccbb35b57c0dfbbfbd31b1625a257effdab4aaf267306aa623c0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13a32e8e68cc-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 43,
              "start": 43
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Cole, the respondent suggests the injunction could be limited to defamatory speech of a similar nature designed to extort."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Cole",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13a32e8e68ccccbb35b57c0dfbbfbd31b1625a257effdab4aaf267306aa623c0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13a32e8e68cc-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 49,
              "start": 49
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Cole, the respondent also proposes narrowing the injunction by striking subparagraphs (ii) and (iii) of paragraph\u202f2."
      }
    ],
